    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c5ba9c10_4a28c8cd",
        "filename": "driver/tcpm/rt1715.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-11T23:00:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e  RT1715_REG_CTRL2 is register 0x81 and the default value is 3Eh. It sets the threshold count for BMC signal to recognize \"0\" and \"1\". RT1715 will start to count between two transients. If it counts over than the threshold, RT1715 recognize as BMC \"0\". If it counts less than the threshold, RT1715 recognize as BMC \"1\". It is modified from 3Eh to 36h for less threshold.\nIf I understand correctly, this entire register is one field, and the value of that field is the count (of time?) after which the PHY will recognize a BMC 1 if it has seen a second transition and a BMC 0 if it has not seen a second transition.\n* Does the counter represent a duration?\n* If so, how much time is one unit increase/decrease?\n* What is the default duration, and what is the new duration?\n* See above question about your use of the word \"transient.\"",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 77,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 80,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "7205c416814e2bf3dfc87c539317f3742e005d96",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
