      "key": {
        "uuid": "9727f33a_77df2eef",
        "filename": "driver/tcpm/rt1715.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1476372
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-12T09:19:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I understand correctly, this entire register is one field, and the value of that field is the count (of time?) after which the PHY will recognize a BMC 1 if it has seen a second transition and a BMC 0 if it has not seen a second transition.\n\tYes. The entire 0x81 is for this setting.\n\nDoes the counter represent a duration?\n\tYes. it present a time duration.\nIf so, how much time is one unit increase/decrease?\n\tThe one unit is 0.04167us.\nWhat is the default duration, and what is the new duration?\n\tThe default duration is 62*0.04167us\u003d2.67us.\n\tThe new duration is 54*0.04167us\u003d2.25us.",
      "parentUuid": "c5ba9c10_4a28c8cd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 77,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 80,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "7205c416814e2bf3dfc87c539317f3742e005d96",
